.Dd October 2, 2026
.Dt SECCOMP 2
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm seccomp
.Nd filter a thread's system calls
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In linux/seccomp.h
.In linux/filter.h
.Ft int
.Fn syscall SYS_seccomp "unsigned int operation" "unsigned int flags" "void *args"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn seccomp
gives the calling thread a filter of its system calls.
A filter is a classic BPF program that reads
.Vt struct seccomp_data ,
the call's number, the architecture, which is
.Dv AUDIT_ARCH_I386 ,
the address of the instruction after the call, and its six arguments
widened to 64 bits, and returns an action in its high 16 bits and data in
the low 16.
A thread keeps a chain of filters, newest first; every filter judges each
call, and the action of highest precedence is taken:
.Bl -tag -width "SECCOMP_RET_KILL_PROCESS"
.It Dv SECCOMP_RET_KILL_PROCESS
The process ends as killed by
.Dv SIGSYS ,
with a core where it may leave one.
.It Dv SECCOMP_RET_KILL_THREAD
The thread ends as killed by
.Dv SIGSYS ,
and the process with it when it is the last.
.It Dv SECCOMP_RET_TRAP
The call does not run;
.Dv SIGSYS
is posted, with
.Va si_code
.Dv SYS_SECCOMP ,
.Va si_call_addr ,
.Va si_syscall
and
.Va si_arch
of the call, and the data in
.Va si_errno .
EAX holds the call's number for the handler, which may store a result
there.
A blocked or ignored
.Dv SIGSYS
kills the process.
.It Dv SECCOMP_RET_ERRNO
The call does not run and fails with the data as its error, at most 4095.
.It Dv SECCOMP_RET_TRACE
The thread's tracer, which set
.Dv PTRACE_O_TRACESECCOMP ,
gets a
.Dv PTRACE_EVENT_SECCOMP
stop with the data; the call it then leaves runs unless it gave -1 as its
number, after the filters judge it again.
Without such a tracer the call fails with
.Er ENOSYS .
.It Dv SECCOMP_RET_LOG , Dv SECCOMP_RET_ALLOW
The call runs.
.El
.Pp
A program may load the words of
.Vt struct seccomp_data
and its length, compute in its accumulator and index register with
sixteen scratch words, jump forward and return; a division by a zero
register ends it with 0.
.Pp
The operations:
.Bl -tag -width "SECCOMP_GET_ACTION_AVAIL"
.It Dv SECCOMP_SET_MODE_STRICT
With no flags and a null
.Fa args ,
leave the thread only
.Xr read 2 ,
.Xr write 2 ,
.Xr exit 2
and
.Xr sigreturn 2 ;
any other call kills the process with
.Dv SIGKILL ,
where Linux kills the thread alone.
.It Dv SECCOMP_SET_MODE_FILTER
Add the filter the
.Vt struct sock_fprog
at
.Fa args
describes, of at most 4096 instructions.
The caller must have set no_new_privs or be privileged.
.Dv SECCOMP_FILTER_FLAG_TSYNC
gives every thread of the process the caller's new chain, which each must
already share, and returns the id of a thread that does not;
.Dv SECCOMP_FILTER_FLAG_TSYNC_ESRCH
returns
.Er ESRCH
in its place.
.Dv SECCOMP_FILTER_FLAG_LOG
and
.Dv SECCOMP_FILTER_FLAG_SPEC_ALLOW
are accepted and change nothing.
.It Dv SECCOMP_GET_ACTION_AVAIL
Return 0 when the action at
.Fa args
is one of those above.
.It Dv SECCOMP_GET_NOTIF_SIZES
Store Linux's sizes of the structures of the notification interface.
.El
.Pp
A child of
.Xr fork 2
or
.Xr clone 2
has its parent's mode and chain, and
.Xr execve 2
keeps them.
.Xr prctl 2
has the same through
.Dv PR_SET_SECCOMP
and
.Dv PR_GET_SECCOMP ,
and
.Pa /proc/ Ns Ar pid Ns Pa /status
reports the mode and the number of filters.
.Ss Differences from Linux
There is no notification interface:
.Dv SECCOMP_FILTER_FLAG_NEW_LISTENER
is refused, and a filter that returns
.Dv SECCOMP_RET_USER_NOTIF
fails the call with
.Er ENOSYS ,
as on Linux without a listener.
.Ss System call interface
The i386 system call number is 354.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
0 on success; for
.Dv SECCOMP_FILTER_FLAG_TSYNC ,
the id of a thread that cannot take the chain.
On failure -1 with
.Va errno
set.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EACCES
A filter from a caller with neither no_new_privs nor privilege.
.It Bq Er EFAULT
.Fa args
or the program cannot be read.
.It Bq Er EINVAL
An unknown operation or flag, an empty or longer program, an instruction
a filter may not have, a jump past the end, a last instruction that is
not a return, or a filter added in the strict mode.
.It Bq Er ENOMEM
The chain would pass 32768 instructions, each filter counted with four
more.
.It Bq Er EOPNOTSUPP
An action
.Dv SECCOMP_GET_ACTION_AVAIL
does not have.
.It Bq Er ESRCH
A thread that cannot take the chain, with
.Dv SECCOMP_FILTER_FLAG_TSYNC_ESRCH .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr prctl 2 ,
.Xr ptrace 2 ,
.Xr proc 5
